## Why This Is Asked
Path auto-complete is a common editor feature; it probes practical data-structure trade-offs beyond textbooks.

## Key Concepts
- Trie with per-node children map
- Prefix search via traversal then DFS for completions
- Memory sharing of prefixes and separator handling

## Code Example
```javascript
class TrieNode {
  constructor() {
    this.next = new Map();
    this.isEnd = false;
  }
}
class PathTrie {
  constructor() { this.root = new TrieNode(); }
  insertPath(path) {
    let node = this.root;
    for (const ch of path) {
      if (!node.next.has(ch)) node.next.set(ch, new TrieNode());
      node = node.next.get(ch);
    }
    node.isEnd = true;
  }
  autocomplete(prefix, maxResults) {
    let node = this.root;
    for (const ch of prefix) {
      if (!node.next.has(ch)) return [];
      node = node.next.get(ch);
    }
    const results = [];
    const dfs = (cur, built) => {
      if (results.length >= maxResults) return;
      if (cur.isEnd) results.push(prefix + built);
      for (const [ch, child] of cur.next) dfs(child, built + ch);
    };
    dfs(node, "");
    return results;
  }
}
```

